[{:db/id "830ad737-81e3-515d-810c-86375e9cc662" :answer/id #uuid "830ad737-81e3-515d-810c-86375e9cc662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}+C}{5{(x-6)}^{1/4}})}^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "198e90de-3051-575c-bc22-01521b0d1075" :answer/id #uuid "198e90de-3051-575c-bc22-01521b0d1075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{C{(x-6)}^{1/2}-2}{4{(x-6)}^{1/2}})}^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8d613153-ad03-5279-a752-55d311e9f54d" :answer/id #uuid "8d613153-ad03-5279-a752-55d311e9f54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{(x-6)}^{1/4}+C}{4{(x-6)}^{9/4}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" :answer/id #uuid "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}})}^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "347f99a3-0ba6-5adf-a322-65df926c05e0" :answer/id #uuid "347f99a3-0ba6-5adf-a322-65df926c05e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{(x-6)}^{5/4}+C}{3{(x-6)}^{1/4}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3e561d6b-d4ae-5cce-a550-57e45ec5f9c0" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e561d6b-d4ae-5cce-a550-57e45ec5f9c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["830ad737-81e3-515d-810c-86375e9cc662" "198e90de-3051-575c-bc22-01521b0d1075" "8d613153-ad03-5279-a752-55d311e9f54d" "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" "347f99a3-0ba6-5adf-a322-65df926c05e0"] :answer-field/correct "36de1601-f8d7-5c58-8370-c2c78395ace6" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4c866423-3d16-5bfb-95b6-2aad67327bbd" :question/id #uuid "4c866423-3d16-5bfb-95b6-2aad67327bbd" :question/problem "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n(x-6)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={(x-6)}^{2}{y}^{3/4}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $x-6>0$. Choose constants and intervals on which all displayed real expressions are defined. Take $y>0$.\n\n{{selection}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y={(x-6)}^{2}{y}^{3/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y}{(x-6)} & =(x-6){y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)={(x-6)}^{-1},\\,q(x)=(x-6),\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{(x-6)}^{-1}{y}^{1/4}=(x-6).\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+{(x-6)}^{-1}z=(x-6)\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-1}z=\\frac{(x-6)}{4}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is now in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (x-6)},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{(x-6)}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (x-6)})\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{(1/4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-6)} \\\\  & ={(x-6)}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={(x-6)}^{1/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-1}z) & ={(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot (\\frac{(x-6)}{4}) \\\\ {(x-6)}^{1/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-6)}^{-3/4}z & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{(x-6)}^{1/4}) & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{(x-6)}^{1/4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{(x-6)}^{5/4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{(x-6)}^{1/4} & =\\frac{1}{9}{(x-6)}^{9/4}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=9{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{1/4}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/4}=\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}}\\,⇒\\,y={(\\frac{{(x-6)}^{9/4}+C}{9{(x-6)}^{1/4}})}^{4}\\,.\n$$\n\nThese are the nonzero real solutions on the specified intervals; exclude denominator zeros and restrict constants and intervals to the real branches used above. Since $z=y^{1/4}>0$, retain only intervals where the displayed expression for $z$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["3e561d6b-d4ae-5cce-a550-57e45ec5f9c0"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "ef3ede6a-24f7-5984-96b5-eb1a91ac16d8" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186147454.py"} [:db/add 17592186147454 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186147454 :knowledge-point/questions ["4c866423-3d16-5bfb-95b6-2aad67327bbd"]} [:db/ensure 17592186147454 :knowledge-point/validate]]
